---
title: "5 · Email content and templates"
description: Change the wording of one request's emails, and keep the firm's email templates for signers and CC recipients.
sidebar:
  order: 6
  label: "5 · Email content and templates"
---

Signers and CC recipients receive four kinds of email: **Invitation**, **Reminder**, **Completion** and **CC**. Each is built from a template. The greeting, the document list, the button, the security line and the sign-off are added by Operon; a template holds only the subject and the message.

## Change the wording for one request

Select **Email content** on the review screen before sending, or on the request's **Emails** card. Choose the tab of the kind of email (**Invitation**, **Reminder**, **Completion** and, where offered, **CC**), then pick a **Template** or edit the **Subject** and **Message**. **Insert variable** adds a value that is filled in when the email is sent, such as the signer's name. The preview shows the email as the signer will see it. Select **Save**.

The change applies to this request only. **Restore default** goes back to the default template.

## The firm's templates

**Where:** **E-Sign** › **Email templates**. Every user can read the templates; only a tenant admin can change them.

There are two libraries:

| Library | Used by |
|---|---|
| **Case signing** | Signing steps inside a case. |
| **General** | Signature requests that are not part of a case, such as those sent from **+ New Request**. |

For each kind of email, the library lists its templates. The template marked **Default** is the one a request uses when nothing was saved for it. Templates marked **Platform preset** are provided by Operon and can only be viewed: select **Duplicate** to make your own copy. Your own templates can be changed with **Edit**. **Set as default** makes a template the default; a template that is not the default can be removed with **Delete** (a platform preset cannot). **New template** adds one.

{% screenshot id="e-sign/templates-list" caption="The email templates of the General library." /%}

Deleting a template does not affect requests that already saved their own content.
